  "titles": {
    "_tiers_note": "Seven ACKS domain tiers, ascending by size (barony, march, county, duchy, principality, kingdom, empire) per RAW; the march is a small frontier holding between barony and county. DISPLAY titles are English; the empire ruler displays as the approved foreign term Imperator. The Latinate ruler_native/domain_native pairs (all rhyming on a shared stem) are for NPC dialogue only. The march (frontier) native title is Limitanus/Limitania (from Roman limes/limitanei), leaving Dux/Ducatus for its proper meaning, the duchy. Per-tier family/realm size thresholds come from the ACKS domain rules (acore_axioms_strongholds_and_domains.xml); not reproduced here for IP.",
